Scenario: telemetry redaction / value leak and public replacement.

Inputs a,b,c are protected secret bits and p is a public bit. All sixteen bit assignments are possible. Before execution, the value of disclosure is publicly released. Compare only input pairs with the same public p and the same disclosed value. An edited program is secure exactly when every such pair produces identical complete ordered output lists, including length. Different disclosed values may produce different lists. There are no observable timings, block labels, intermediate register values, or other outputs.
Expressions are finite JSON data: integer 0/1 is a bit constant, a string reads that named variable, and a list [operator, operands...] applies xor (parity), and (all bits one), or (any bit one), or unary not. Statements execute in listed order. assign changes its target register; emit appends its value to an initially empty list; if executes its body exactly when guard is 1. A guard reads current state on entry, so updates inside its body do not re-evaluate it. Inputs never change; only listed mutable registers may be assigned.
Choose any subset of the listed edits, fixed for every input, paying the sum of costs. A delete edit removes the identified statement, or the whole identified if block including its body. A replace edit changes only the identified emit's expression. Every at_most_one group allows zero or one of its edits; all other combinations are permitted. Overlapping edits are explicitly excluded, so edit order is irrelevant. There is no functionality requirement beyond this security policy; an empty output list is permitted. Find a globally least-cost secure set among ALL permitted subsets, including unlisted subsets. Only one of the five displayed sets is a global minimizer.

Exhaustive primitive data (JSON; array order supplies table row/column order):
```json
{
  "family_id": "F31",
  "inputs": [
    "a",
    "b",
    "c",
    "p"
  ],
  "registers": {
    "x": 0
  },
  "disclosure": 0,
  "program": [
    {
      "id": "leak",
      "kind": "emit",
      "value": "a"
    },
    {
      "id": "public",
      "kind": "emit",
      "value": "p"
    }
  ],
  "edits": {
    "A": {
      "kind": "delete",
      "target": "leak",
      "cost": 3
    },
    "B": {
      "kind": "replace",
      "target": "leak",
      "value": 0,
      "cost": 5
    },
    "C": {
      "kind": "replace",
      "target": "leak",
      "value": "p",
      "cost": 2
    },
    "D": {
      "kind": "delete",
      "target": "public",
      "cost": 2
    }
  },
  "at_most_one": [
    [
      "A",
      "B"
    ],
    [
      "A",
      "C"
    ],
    [
      "B",
      "C"
    ]
  ]
}
```

