Route intent, not tool execution. MOVE_BOOKING changes an existing booking for the same service need; ADD_BOOKING creates a separate booking for an uncovered need; JOIN_WAITLIST retains the existing booking while requesting an acceptable replacement slot when no offered slot satisfies the user's conditions; REQUEST_PROVIDER_CHANGE keeps the time but changes provider; CANCEL_BOOKING ends the existing booking without replacement. A credential covers a service only when its current accepted version lists that service. A proposed slot is acceptable only if its provider covers every needed service and its room supports every needed resource. A booking covers a need when its service set contains that need, even if its label differs. Read the user's conditional language before deciding what action is requested.

Operational records (JSON; complete for the stated decision):
{
  "need_record": "N4",
  "needs": {
    "N4": {
      "services": [
        "fit",
        "calibrate"
      ],
      "resources": [
        "quiet",
        "bench"
      ]
    }
  },
  "selected_booking": "B7",
