Select the one primary service destination the customer requests now: DELIVERY traces an unreceived unit; INVOICE supplies the billing document; REPAIR repairs covered faulty goods; REPLACE supplies replacement goods; RETURN arranges goods back for money back. Invoice-line aliases identify physical units, which count once. A faulty unit is covered if and only if its inspection_ticket_day is on or before its model's inclusive warranty cutoff. Tickets also exist for inspected units found not faulty; their dates matter only if faulty=true. Compatible replacement SKUs are exhaustive. Stock is shared, and each stock unit can replace at most one physical unit. The customer applies the first matching condition to the selected batch: trace any selected unreceived unit; otherwise if none is faulty, supply the invoice; otherwise if all faulty selected units are covered, repair them; otherwise if one stock assignment replaces EVERY uncovered faulty selected unit simultaneously, replace that uncovered batch and defer covered repairs; otherwise return ALL faulty selected units for money back. Only this one primary outcome is requested today. No unlisted stock, request, unit or permission exists. The requested batch is exactly the physical units named by the kept invoice-line manifest. Ignore all other units.

